<title>LATVIA: Latvian trade deficit rises in Jan-Oct.</title>
<headline>Latvian trade deficit rises in Jan-Oct.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's trade deficit, measured in real prices that do not strip out inflation, rose to 360.9 million lats in January-October, the statistics committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Inflation in October was 1.2 percent on a monthly basis and 15.7 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p> LATVIAN TRADE  Jan-Oct '96   Jan-Sept '96   Jan-Oct '95</p>
<p> Exports	    653.1	     579.10	   764.22</p>
<p> Imports		1.01 billion  894.12	   559.14</p>
<p> Balance	   -360.9	    -315.02	  -205.10</p>
<p>NOTE -- All figures in millions of lats unless stated otherwise.</p>
<p>Largest export destination as percentage of total exports versus same period last year</p>
<p>Russia -  22.9 (24.9)</p>
<p>Germany - 13.9 (14.3)</p>
<p>Britain - 10.7 (9.5)</p>
<p>Largest source of imports as percentage of total exports versus the same period last year:</p>
<p>Russia -  18.9 (21.2)</p>
<p>Germany - 14.1 (15.6)</p>
<p>Finland -  9.5 (10.5)</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
